  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: 'Do you hate yourself?'",
  "description": "The text 'do you hate yourself?' is a rhetorical question used to imply that the Black man is self-hating or has low self-esteem, which is a common anti-Black stereotype. This stereotype suggests that Black people are inherently flawed or inferior, and that their struggles are due to their own internal issues rather than systemic racism or societal oppression.",
